WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.040
 In the add co-instructors
  and teaching assistants video, 

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.840
 we saw how to add members 
  to our workspace one by one. 

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.800
 But what if we want to add a large number 
  of individuals to our space at once? 

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.640
 There are several ways to add multiple 
  members to your workspace at once. 

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.880
 And in this video 
  we'll go through the sharing link option. 

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.720
 Please check out the 
  rscloud package video 

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.120
 if you're interested in learning  

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.520
 how to add multiple members via 
  the RStudio Cloud API.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.120
 To add multiple individuals 
  to our workspace 

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.200
 let's click on the members button 
  at the top of our workspace 

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.520
 and then click on options 
  to open the access menu. From here

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.560
 let's invite multiple individuals 
  using the sharing link. 

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.400
 This method will give us a link 
  that we can distribute via email 

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.880
 or on a course web page, 

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.720
 allowing all of our learners to access the 
  workspace on RStudio Cloud.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.240
 For the initial role 
  we'll choose contributors,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.400
 and then take a look at the permissions 
  at the bottom of the page. 

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.280
 We can choose what contributors 
  are allowed to do within the workspace 

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.480
 by selecting or de-selecting 
  the options presented. 

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.880
 Once we've made our selections 
  we can click on copy 

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.400
 sharing link and distribute it as needed. 

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.360
 Once all of our learners 
  have joined the shared workspace 

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.800
 we can disable the existing link 
  by resetting the sharing link 

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.960
 or by setting our workspace 
  to invitation required, 

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.720
 which will mean new learners 
  to the workspace will have to be added via 

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.760
 the add member button from within 
  the member section of our workspace. 

